== 4. the F2 pin moved rather than grew (non-blocking) ==

M5b survives: the `readFileSync` catch's `continue` is no longer reached by any fixture,
because `00-unreadable.md` (a directory) is now intercepted by `lstatSync(p).isFile()` before
the read. The spec's property — "a brief that cannot be read is skipped without aborting" — is
still pinned, now by M5a/M5c on the lstat path, so coverage did not shrink for the behaviour;
what is unpinned is the specific branch round 2's fix pinned.

I am NOT blocking on it, deliberately. The only fixture that reaches that catch is a
permission-denied regular file, and mode bits do not deny root — a chmod-000 row silently stops
pinning anything under a root CI, which trades a real flake for a theoretical pin. The honest
options are (a) a root-aware chmod fixture, or (b) one comment line saying the catch is
unpinned defence-in-depth covering the lstat->read TOCTOU window. Either is fine; neither is
worth a round.

